A tick that charges the thread running on lent time rather than the thread that lends it.
The payer's account is no longer counted to the core's count.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a tick did not cost the thread whose turn it was a tick less its units

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -753,7 +753,7 @@ void irq_drop(struct cap *signalled)
 static void tick_advance(uint32_t ticks)
 {
     struct core *core = core_self();
-    struct thread *payer = turn_payer(core);
+    struct thread *payer = core->turn;
     uint32_t owed = sched_ticks + ticks - core->ticks;
     core->wake_stale = true;
